  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **While My Guitar Gently Weeps**: back after 35 archived shows (742 days); rare: 3 archived performances [5]\n- **Fire Eater**: back after 235 archived shows (4404 days); rare: 4 archived performances [5]\n- **The Swamp**: back after 31 archived shows (736 days); rare: 6 archived performances [5]\n- **Upshot**: back after 116 archived shows (1967 days); rare: 7 archived performances [5]\n- **Pungee**: rare: 5 archived performances [5]\n- **Keep On Marching**: rare: 3 archived performances [5]\n- **He Bite Me (The Dragon)**: rare: 4 archived performances [5]\n- **On The Road To Charlie Parker**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2015-03-19.cmc622xt.sbd.matrix.flac24** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 19 songs; 168 min [1]\n- **soulive2015-03-19.cmc622xt.sbd.matrix.flac16**: matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 19 songs; 168 min [2]\n- **soulive2015-03-19.140s-mk4s.mix.flac16**: source not stated; 19 songs; 166 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The show was Night 6 of the Bowlive VI run at Brooklyn Bowl [1]\n- The Shady Horns joined the band: Ryan Zoidis on saxophones and Eric Bloom on trumpet [3]\n- George Porter Jr. guested on bass and vocals, and Anders Osborne on guitar and vocals [3]\n- The reviewer says this night was part of the Bowlive run and asks about recordings of the other nights [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2015-03-19.cmc622xt.sbd.matrix.flac24**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: On Stage Audience/SBD Matrix [1]. Also: Schoeps cmc622xt on-stage mics through Sonosax preamp and Apogee converter to Sound Devices 744T, matrixed with a Digidesign/Avid Profile soundboard feed, recorded at 24/96; Both sources were time-aligned in SoundForge, then mixed and rendered in Vegas Pro 13; this is the 24-bit release, with a separate 16-bit version [1]\n- **soulive2015-03-19.cmc622xt.sbd.matrix.flac16**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: On Stage Audience/SBD Matrix [2]. Also: Matrix of Schoeps on-stage mics and soundboard feed, both captured on a Sound Devices 744T at 24/96, mixed in Vegas Pro 13; Downconverted to 16-bit/44.1 using iZotope sample-rate conversion and MBIT+ dither, then converted to FLAC through CDWav; Eric McRoberts recorded, mixed and mastered this version [2]\n- **soulive2015-03-19.140s-mk4s.mix.flac16**: taped by Frank D'Auria; transferred by Frank D'Auria; source: Neumann SKM140s>Edirol R44 + Schoeps CMC5/MK4>Sonosax SX-M2>Edirol R44 [3]",
